<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">San Pedro Sula</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1536">1536</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">San Pedro Sula is the second-largest city of Honduras and its main industrial and commercial centre, in the fertile Sula valley of the north-west. Founded by the Spanish in 1536, it grew rapidly from the late nineteenth century with the railway and the banana companies, and later with manufacturing, including garment assembly plants. In the 2010s gang violence made it one of the world's most violent cities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-pedro-sula.jpg" alt="San Pedro Sula" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JVC3ETA · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Collage_of_San_Pedro_Sula_Honduras.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
